From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luca Tramonti
Date: Sun, 26 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Option to limit Virtual Keyboard to Tablet Mode

Adds an option to the Virtual Keyboard page that makes the virtual keyboard
appear only when the device is in Tablet Mode (a convertible flipped back, or
Tablet Mode enabled in the General Behavior page). The option is hidden and
not honored if the device doesn't support Tablet Mode.

This is KWin merge request 8592 by Luca Tramonti, "Option to limit Virtual
Keyboard to Tablet Mode", as it stood on 2026-11-15: open, not a draft, eight
commits ending in bef58762b9, needing a rebase on master. It is carried here
on 6.7.4, where it does not apply as written:
- the key, its default and its meaning are the merge request's: kwinrc,
  [Wayland] InputMethodTabletOnly, true, honored only while tablet mode is
  available, read through a KConfigWatcher;
- InputMethod::shouldShowOnActive() of 6.7.4 has the visibility modes of merge
  request 8509 (Never, touch and tablet, any input), so the condition is put
  in front of them: outside tablet mode nothing is shown, in tablet mode the
  chosen visibility mode decides;
- the page's footer has the merge request's form, "Show automatically: Only when
  in Tablet Mode"; its "Manage Tablet Mode" button is left out;
- the page shows the form when KWin itself says tablet mode is available
  (org.kde.KWin.TabletModeManager, tabletModeAvailable), read by the page's own
  class: Kirigami.Settings.tabletModeAvailable, which the merge request uses,
  answered false in the settings program while KWin answered true.

Origin: other, https://invent.kde.org/plasma/kwin/-/merge_requests/8592
Author: Luca Tramonti
Forwarded: not-needed
Applied-Upstream: no, an open merge request
Last-Update: 2026-11-15

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5-2
